"""##Standard Normal Variate (SNV) & De-trending (DT)
(**Performed on log(1/R) spectral data**)

- Removes multiplicative interferences of scatter and particle size (Barnes et al., 1989)

$X_{SNV}=(X-\bar{X})/SD$
- Mitigate variance in slope and **divergence** between samples varying in size
- Typically Performed on log(1/R)
- Combined with de-trending (DT) accounting for variation in baseline shift and curvilinearity, generally found in reflectance spectra of powdered or densely packed samples, with the use of a second-degree polynomial regression to remove low frequency baseline drifts by fitting and subtracting

$p(\lambda)=a_0+a_1\lambda+a_2^2\lambda^2$

$X_{SNV-detrended}=X_{SNV}-p(\lambda)$
- Standardize variation in curvilinearity in 1100-2500 nm range of SNV spectra associated with particle size and packing density
- De-trending w/o SNV to visualize shape differences
"""

import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

def SNV(X):
  return (X - np.mean(X, axis=0) / np.std(X, axis=0, ddof=1))

transform_SNV_spiru_data = transform_spiru_data.copy()
